==English==
{{wp}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|conterpart}}, {{m|enm|countre parte|t=duplicate of a legal document}}, equivalent to {{com|en|counter-|part}}. Compare {{cog|fro|contrepartie}}, itself from {{m|fro|contre||facing, opposite}} (from {{cog|la|contra||against}}) + {{m|fro|partie||copy of a person or thing}} (originally past participle of {{m|la|partīre||to divide}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkaʊntəˌpɑːt/|a=UK}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkaʊntɚˌpɑɹt/|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-counterpart.ogg|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Either of two [[part]]s that [[fit together#Verb|fit together]] or otherwise [[complement#Verb|complement]] one another.
#: {{nearsyn|en|complement#Noun|mate#Noun}}
#: {{ux|en|Those brass knobs and their hollow '''counterparts''' interlock perfectly.}}
#* {{RQ:en:New York Times|date=November 7, 2012|author=Matt Bai|title=Winning a Second Term, Obama Will Confront Familiar Headwinds|url=http://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/us/politics/in-president-obamas-second-term-familiar-challenges.html?pagewanted=all&_r=0
|passage=Mr. Obama never found a generational '''counterpart''' among conservatives in Congress like Paul D. Ryan or Eric Cantor; instead, there was a mutual animosity.}}
# {{lb|en|legal}} A [[duplicate]] of a legal document.
#: {{hyper|en|copy#Noun|duplicate#Noun}}
# One who or that which [[resemble]]s another. {{rfex|en}}
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:counterpart}}
# One who or that which has [[corresponding]] [[function]]s or [[characteristic]]s.
#: {{nearsyn|en|q1=each contextually synonymous|opposite number|counterparty|opponent|homolog|homotype|equivalent|partner|vis-à-vis}}
#: {{ux|en|Her French '''counterpart''' attended the meeting via video call.}}
#: {{ux|en|The two companies are working together with their respective '''counterparts''' in Asia.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en
|date=November 12, 2011
|author=
|title=International friendly: England 1-0 Spain
|work=BBC Sport
|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/15693231.stm
|page=
|passage=England's attacking impetus was limited to one shot from Lampard that was comfortably collected by keeper Iker Casillas, but for all Spain's domination of the ball his England '''counterpart''' Joe Hart was unemployed.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20120201060013/http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/15693231.stm|archivedate=1 February 2012}}
# {{lb|en|palaeontology}} Either half of a flattened [[fossil]] when the rock has split along the plane of the fossil.

